# LLM model recommendation (gated)

You cannot switch the user’s chat model. When this rule applies, recommend one primary + one fallback once, then continue.

## Hard skip (never load or tip)

Do **not** read this file or emit a **Model tip** when:

- Cursor **Ask** mode (questions only)
- Simple bug fixes (clear repro, one path, no architecture)
- Simple design / UI polish (copy, spacing, icon, color, one component)
- Tiny Agent edits, renames, “what does this do?”, or follow-ups mid-task

Default: **stay silent** on models. Silence saves tokens.

## When to apply

Only if **both** are true:

1. Work is clearly **above** simple bug / simple design / Ask, **and**
2. Either:
   - **Plan mode** is active (or user asked to **make a plan** for non-trivial work), or
   - The prompt is obviously multi-system, security/RBAC-heavy, roadmap-batch, schema+API+UI, or sticky/ambiguous

Then: read this file once; one tip; do not repeat every turn.

## Sophistication ladder

| Level | Signals | Prefer |
|-------|---------|--------|
| **Standard** | Non-trivial feature API+UI, schema migration, permission seed, audit path, CI with real diagnosis | **Claude Sonnet 5.5** (Medium). Fallbacks: **Opus 5.5**, **GPT-5.5** / **GPT-5.6 Sol**, **Codex 5.3** (CI/code) |
| **High** | Roadmap batch, RBAC/security review, multi-system, architecture trade-offs | **Claude Opus 4.8** (High). Fallbacks: **Fable 5.1**, **Muse Wonder** |
| **Extra high** | Ambiguous hard design, deep tenant/security blast radius | **Claude Opus 4.7** (Extra High). Fallback: **Opus 4.8** |

Skip recommending **Lite** models in this rule — those tasks should not trigger the tip at all (user can keep Auto / current model).

Also OK at Standard: **Gemini 4 Argon** / **Gemini 3.1 Pro**; **Grok 4.7** only if the user asks for speed on an already-complex plan.

## Plan template → tip?

| Template | Tip? |
|----------|------|
| **F**, tiny **G**/**H** only | **No** — too simple |
| **A**, **D**, **E**, **I**, **J**, non-trivial **G**/**H** | Yes → Standard |
| **B**, **C**, **A+E**, multi-letter | Yes → High (Extra high if deep **C**) |
| **K** | Tip only if signals are clearly Standard+ |

## Reply shape

> **Model tip:** use **Claude Sonnet 5.5** for this (standard feature). Fallback: Opus 5.5. Switch in the model picker if you want.

Never claim you switched models. Never invent names outside the picker list above.
